  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true when testing the stability of Euler's method on the test equation ${y}^{\u2032}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda =5,$ and step size $\u0394x?$\n\n- The update formula can be written as ${y}_{n+1}=(1-5\u0394x)^{n}{y}_{n}.$\n- The method is stable for $|1-5\u0394x|<1.$\n- The method is stable for step size $\u0394x=0.2.$\n- The method is **unstable** for step size $\u0394x=0.25.$",
